Presidential elections were held in [[Georgia (country)|Georgia]] on 5 November (or 6 November<ref>{{Cite journal |date=1996 |title=Election Watch |url=https://muse.jhu.edu/pub/1/article/697484 |journal=Journal of Democracy |volume=7 |issue=1 |issn=1086-3214}}</ref>) 1995.<ref>[[Dieter Nohlen]], Florian Grotz & Christof Hartmann (2001) ''Elections in Asia: A data handbook, Volume I'', p382 {{ISBN|0-19-924958-X}}</ref> The result was a victory for [[Eduard Shevardnadze]] of the [[Union of Citizens of Georgia]], who received 77% of the vote, with a 68% turnout.<ref>Nohlen ''et al.'', p402</ref>

